  "request": "Support all text formats including files often larger than 1 GB; avoid full-buffer GUI memory and preserve whole-file edits/saves",
  "changes": [
    "Disk-backed Rust byte piece table, 64-bit positions, 64KiB scalar-aligned pages, no mmap or full-file text/index",
    "Native bounded input projection, byte/page navigation and literal whole-file search; independent immutable fragment syntax actor so disk saves cannot queue-block highlighting",
    "Original-encoding/BOM complete chunked atomic export, version/permission/metadata fences, cancellation before commit",
    "Transactional cross-page undo with prepared page, bounded removed+inserted history frozen before save, no retained old full-file inodes",
    "Revision-based conservative input reservations, aggregate native multi-range and normal-document budgets; capacity refusal keeps valid edits saveable",
    "Full-text LSP/workspace modifications explicitly reject disk-backed page targets; global-line navigation reports unavailable rather than applying local offsets",
    "Separate complete preview 32MiB source/64MiB output with pre-parser Markdown density guard, cooperative cancellation, visible failure placeholder and no false linked scrolling"
  ],
